#
# THE COMMIT OF muir THIS ONE IS HELD TO.
#
# Every reference trace in `golden/` is muir's own behaviour written down, so
# a commit here means nothing without the commit of muir it was generated
# against: the same generator over a different muir is a different reference,
# and a check that passes against one may fail against the other for reasons
# that have nothing to do with the fabric.  CLAUDE.md carried this as a rule
# about when to pull --- "at slice boundaries, never mid-slice" --- which is
# discipline where it should be a fact in a file.
#
# `make muir-pin` says whether the muir beside this repository is this commit,
# and `make check` runs it and warns.  CI checks this commit out rather than
# muir's main branch, so the pair is tested and not whatever main happens to
# be that morning.
#
# TO MOVE IT: pull muir, write the new SHA here, `rm -f build/*.golden`,
# `make check`, and commit the pin and any trace that changed TOGETHER, with
# what moved in the message.  A trace that changes under a muir bump is the
# most interesting thing that can happen here and must not arrive silently in
# somebody else's commit.
dad7249d79acdbf4bca6b61f4ade4c4a17f4d244
